edicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) Executive Order No. 10898 of December 2,1960, and Executive  \nOrder No. 10986 of January 12, 1962, are revoked.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 4543, PDF pages 5-5; Sec. 1(b)","sha256":"f0165f445a626e54815576c9ae62aaf647866b1a93638418d0837398cff43aba","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-03-14/pdf/FR-1970-03-14.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11515#sec1(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Execuitve Order No. 11382 of November 28,1967, is amended by  \ndeleting section 8.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 4543, PDF pages 5-5; Sec. 1(c)","sha256":"f0165f445a626e54815576c9ae62aaf647866b1a93638418d0837398cff43aba","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-03-14/pdf/FR-1970-03-14.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11515#sec1(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"S ec. 2. Interagency Committee on International Athletics.  The In­\nteragency Committee on International Athletics is terminated and  \nExecutive Order No. 11117 of August 13, 1963, is revoked.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 4543, PDF pages 5-5; Sec. 2","sha256":"f0165f445a626e54815576c9ae62aaf647866b1a93638418d0837398cff43aba","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-03-14/pdf/FR-1970-03-14.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11515#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"S ec. 3. Presidents Committee on Manpower.  The President’s Com­\nmittee on Manpower is hereby terminated and Executive Order No.  \n11152 of April 15,1964, is revoked.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 4543, PDF pages 5-5; Sec. 3","sha256":"f0165f445a626e54815576c9ae62aaf647866b1a93638418d0837398cff43aba","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-03-14/pdf/FR-1970-03-14.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11515#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"S ec. 4. Ohio River Bridge Tragedy.  There is hereby terminated the  \ntask force established by the President by announcement made on  \nDecember 19,1967, in connection with the collapse of the Ohio River  \nBridge on Highway U.S. 35 connecting Gallipolis, Ohio, and Pt.  \nPleasant, West Virginia.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 4543, PDF pages 5-5; Sec. 4","sha256":"f0165f445a626e54815576c9ae62aaf647866b1a93638418d0837398cff43aba","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-03-14/pdf/FR-1970-03-14.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11515#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"S ec. 5. Medal of Freedom.  Executive Order No. 9586 of July 6,1945,  \nas amended, is hereby further amended:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 4543, PDF pages 5-5; Sec. 5 (lead-in)","sha256":"f0165f445a626e54815576c9ae62aaf647866b1a93638418d0837398cff43aba","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-03-14/pdf/FR-1970-03-14.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11515#sec5","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(1) By substituting for subsection (b) of section 2 the following:\n“(b)  The President may select for the award of the Medal any person  \nrecommended to the President for award of the Medal or any person  \nselected by the President upon his own initiative.”","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 4543, PDF pages 5-5; Sec. 5(1)","sha256":"f0165f445a626e54815576c9ae62aaf647866b1a93638418d0837398cff43aba","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-03-14/pdf/FR-1970-03-14.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11515#sec5(1)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(2) By striking out all numbered sections of the order except sections  \n1 and 2.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 4543, PDF pages 5-5; Sec. 5(2)","sha256":"f0165f445a626e54815576c9ae62aaf647866b1a93638418d0837398cff43aba","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-03-14/pdf/FR-1970-03-14.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11515#sec5(2)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"S ec. 6. Winding up of affairs.  Such actions as may be necessary to  \nwind up any outstanding affairs of the bodies terminated by this order  \nshall be carried out by the Bureau of the Budget or by such other  \nagencies as may be designated therefor by the Director of the Bureau  \nof the Budget.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 4543, PDF pages 5-5; Sec. 6","sha256":"f0165f445a626e54815576c9ae62aaf647866b1a93638418d0837398cff43aba","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-03-14/pdf/FR-1970-03-14.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11515#sec6","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 4543, PDF pages 5-5","sha256":"f0165f445a626e54815576c9ae62aaf647866b1a93638418d0837398cff43aba","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-03-14/pdf/FR-1970-03-14.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 10 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: current legal basis not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"yes"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:11515"}
